{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P61073","uniProtkbId":"CXCR4_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"C-X-C chemokine receptor type 4"},"shortNames":[{"value":"CXC-R4"},{"value":"CXCR-4"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"FB22"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Fusin"}},{"fullName":{"value":"HM89"}},{"fullName":{"value":"LCR1"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Leukocyte-derived seven transmembrane domain receptor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8276799"}],"value":"LESTR"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Lipopolysaccharide-associated protein 3"},"shortNames":[{"value":"LAP-3"},{"value":"LPS-associated protein 3"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"NPYRL"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Stromal cell-derived factor 1 receptor"},"shortNames":[{"value":"SDF-1 receptor"}]}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD184"}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"9468539"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:2561"}],"value":"CXCR4"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P70658"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10074102"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10452968"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10644702"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10825158"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11276205"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16725153"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17197449"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18799424"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20048153"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20228059"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20505072"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24912431"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28978524"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"39093700"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8752280"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8752281"}],"value":"Receptor for the C-X-C chemokine CXCL12/SDF-1 that transduces a signal by increasing intracellular calcium ion levels and enhancing MAPK1/MAPK3 activation (PubMed:10074102, PubMed:10452968, PubMed:10644702, PubMed:10825158, PubMed:18799424, PubMed:20048153, PubMed:20505072, PubMed:24912431, PubMed:28978524, PubMed:8752280, PubMed:8752281). Ligand binding causes a conformation change that triggers signaling via guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G proteins) and modulates the activity of downstream effectors, such as adenylate cyclase (PubMed:16725153, PubMed:17197449, PubMed:18799424, PubMed:39093700). CXCR4 is coupled to G(i) G alpha proteins and mediates inhibition of adenylate cyclase (PubMed:17197449, PubMed:39093700). Involved in the AKT signaling cascade (PubMed:24912431). Plays a role in regulation of cell migration, e.g. during wound healing (PubMed:28978524). Also acts as a receptor for extracellular ubiquitin; leading to enhanced intracellular calcium ions and reduced cellular cAMP levels (PubMed:20228059). Binds bacterial lipopolysaccharide (LPS) et mediates LPS-induced inflammatory response, including TNF secretion by monocytes (PubMed:11276205). Involved in hematopoiesis and in cardiac ventricular septum formation (By similarity). Also plays an essential role in vascularization of the gastrointestinal tract, probably by regulating vascular branching and/or remodeling processes in endothelial cells (By similarity). Involved in cerebellar development; in the CNS, could mediate hippocampal-neuron surviva (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10074122"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10756055"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8849450"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8929542"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9427609"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a coreceptor (CD4 being the primary receptor) for human immunodeficiency virus-1/HIV-1 X4 isolates and as a primary receptor for some HIV-2 isolates. Promotes Env-mediated fusion of the virus (PubMed:10074122, PubMed:10756055, PubMed:8849450, PubMed:8929542, PubMed:9427609)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000000106C"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P03971","uniProtkbId":"AMH_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"20861221"}],"value":"Anti-Muellerian hormone"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"20861221"}],"value":"AMH"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8162013"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8872466"}],"value":"Muellerian-inhibiting factor"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"3754790"}],"value":"Muellerian-inhibiting substance"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"3754790"}],"value":"MIS"}]}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:464"}],"value":"AMH"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8162013"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"8872466"}],"value":"MIF"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P27106"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14742691"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20861221"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"34155118"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"3754790"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8469238"}],"value":"The anti-Muellerian hormone (AMH) plays an important role in several reproductive functions (PubMed:14742691, PubMed:34155118, PubMed:3754790, PubMed:8469238). Anti-Muellerian hormone binds and activates AMHR2, its specific type-II receptor, that heterodimerizes with type-I receptors (ACVR1 and BMPR1A) to regulate target gene expression through downstream SMAD protein signal transduction (PubMed:20861221, PubMed:34155118). Produced and secreted by Sertoli cells of the male fetus, anti-Muellerian hormone induces Muellerian duct regression during male fetal sexual differentiation (PubMed:34155118, PubMed:3754790, PubMed:8469238). In female, it is produced by granulosa cells of the preantral and small antral follicles and acts as a negative regulator of the primordial to primary follicle transition and decreases FSH sensitivity of growing follicles (PubMed:14742691). Also plays a role in Leydig cell differentiation and function (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000013C7D0"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P04233","uniProtkbId":"HG2A_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"HLA class II histocompatibility antigen gamma chain"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"HLA-DR antigens-associated invariant chain"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Ia antigen-associated invariant chain"},"shortNames":[{"value":"Ii"}]}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD74"}],"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"1448172"}],"value":"Class-II-associated invariant chain peptide"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"1448172"}],"value":"CLIP"}]}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:1697"}],"value":"CD74"},"synonyms":[{"value":"DHLAG"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"value":"Plays a critical role in MHC class II antigen processing by stabilizing peptide-free class II alpha/beta heterodimers in a complex soon after their synthesis and directing transport of the complex from the endoplasmic reticulum to the endosomal/lysosomal system where the antigen processing and binding of antigenic peptides to MHC class II takes place. Serves as cell surface receptor for the cytokine MIF"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1448172"}],"value":"Binds to the peptide-binding site of MHC class II alpha/beta heterodimers forming an alpha-beta-CLIP complex, thereby preventing the loading of antigenic peptides to the MHC class II complex until its release by HLA-DM in the endosome"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Class-II-associated invariant chain peptide"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P04441"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"32855215"}],"value":"Stabilizes the conformation of mature CTSL by binding to its active site and serving as a chaperone to help maintain a pool of mature enzyme in endocytic compartments and extracellular space of antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Has antiviral activity by stymieing the endosomal entry of Ebola virus and coronaviruses, including SARS-CoV-2 (PubMed:32855215). Disrupts cathepsin-mediated Ebola virus glycoprotein processing, which prevents viral fusion and entry. This antiviral activity is specific to p41 isoform (PubMed:32855215)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform p41"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000012C6BB"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P14174","uniProtkbId":"MIF_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2552447"}],"value":"Macrophage migration inhibitory factor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2552447"}],"value":"MIF"}],"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11439086"}],"value":"5.3.2.1"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P34884"}],"value":"Glycosylation-inhibiting factor"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P34884"}],"value":"GIF"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"L-dopachrome isomerase"}},{"fullName":{"value":"L-dopachrome tautomerase"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17526494"}],"value":"5.3.3.12"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Phenylpyruvate tautomerase"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2552447"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:7097"}],"value":"MIF"},"synonyms":[{"value":"GLIF"},{"value":"MMIF"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11439086"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15908412"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17443469"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17526494"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23776208"}],"value":"Pro-inflammatory cytokine involved in the innate immune response to bacterial pathogens (PubMed:15908412, PubMed:17443469, PubMed:23776208). The expression of MIF at sites of inflammation suggests a role as mediator in regulating the function of macrophages in host defense (PubMed:15908412, PubMed:17443469, PubMed:23776208). Counteracts the anti-inflammatory activity of glucocorticoids (PubMed:15908412, PubMed:17443469, PubMed:23776208). Has phenylpyruvate tautomerase and dopachrome tautomerase activity (in vitro), but the physiological substrate is not known (PubMed:11439086, PubMed:17526494). It is not clear whether the tautomerase activity has any physiological relevance, and whether it is important for cytokine activity (PubMed:11439086, PubMed:17526494)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000005273C"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB unreviewed (TrEMBL)","primaryAccession":"A6MUU8","uniProtkbId":"A6MUU8_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00039619"}],"value":"Macrophage migration inhibitory factor"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00039086"}],"value":"5.3.2.1"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00038932"}],"value":"5.3.3.12"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00042730"}],"value":"L-dopachrome isomerase"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00041631"}],"value":"L-dopachrome tautomerase"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00041912"}],"value":"Phenylpyruvate tautomerase"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000313","source":"EMBL","id":"ABR12395.1"}],"value":"MIF"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00046107"}],"value":"Pro-inflammatory cytokine involved in the innate immune response to bacterial pathogens. The expression of MIF at sites of inflammation suggests a role as mediator in regulating the function of macrophages in host defense. Counteracts the anti-inflammatory activity of glucocorticoids. Has phenylpyruvate tautomerase and dopachrome tautomerase activity (in vitro), but the physiological substrate is not known. It is not clear whether the tautomerase activity has any physiological relevance, and whether it is important for cytokine activity"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000157943F"}},
